  "notes": "{解決|かいけつ} means to solve or resolve a problem or issue. Used as both a noun and suru-verb.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]を{解決|かいけつ}する\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {問題|もんだい}を{解決|かいけつ}する: to solve a problem\n- {解決|かいけつ}{策|さく}: solution, resolution strategy\n- {解決|かいけつ}に{向|む}かう: to move toward resolution\n- {解決|かいけつ}{済|ず}み: resolved, settled\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {解|と}く: to solve (less formal, puzzles/riddles)\n- {解消|かいしょう}: elimination, dissolving (stress, tensions)\n- {解答|かいとう}: answer (to a question)\n\nREGISTER:\nFormal word often used in business and official contexts.",
